out: Usage: djinterp [OPTION]... COMMAND [ARGUMENT]...
out: The djinterp language's command line: its djins and their settings.
out: 
out: Commands:
out:   list                list the djins, a line each
out:   describe            describe a djin: its commands and settings
out:   get                 print settings as statements that load back; every one,
out:                       without a NAME
out:   set                 write settings to the user's settings file
out:   help                display help for a command
out:   completion          print a completion script for a shell
out: 
out: Options:
out:   -q, --quiet         say nothing but errors
out:   -v, --verbose       say more; twice, more again
out:       --color[=WHEN]  colour diagnostics: auto (the default), always or never
out:   -h, --help          display this help and exit
out:       --version       output version information and exit
out: 
out: Exit status:
out:   0  if it did what was asked, and the answer, if one was asked, is yes
out:   1  if it did, and the answer is no
out:   2  if there was trouble: the command line, a file, or the program
